@ykim362 I understand why you want to add this parameter, but Transformers is a bit special in the sense that it computes a single `attention_head_size` from `num_attention_heads` and `hidden_size`. Both having `attention_head_size` as a parameter or having `hidden_size` and `num_attention_heads` as parameters to define `attention_head_size` is fine, but we cannot have both. We decided for the latter option and therefore we should absolutely not add a new `attention_head_size` parameter because this a) breaks backwards compatibility if this parameter replaces `attention_head_size` and `num_heads` and b) leads to a lot of confusing for our users that are used to `num_attention_heads` and `hidden_size`. 

Do we really need this parameter for the new model? 

When one uses our head pruning code the parameters of the module are updated correspondingly: https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/9c0afdaf7b091c341072b432ad6ee17ba7a5016b/src/transformers/models/bert/modeling_bert.py#L319 . It's true that saving and reloading the model might lead to problems if the config is not correctly updated but changing this behavior by using a `attention_head_size` param would lead to the same problem (`num_attention_layers` has to be updated anyways).

