@SaulLu I revised my code so that now the fast tokenizer has the same tokenization strategy as of the slow original one, doing some hacking in the function `_convert_encoding`. 

In particular, I extend the Vietnamese monolingual vocab with all other tokens from the multilingual vocab. So now I have a variant of the multilingual vocab, where the first half stores all tokens from the Vietnamese monolingual vocab and the second half stores the rest, separated by the "mask_token". 

```python
class BartphoConverter(SpmConverter):
    def vocab(self, proto):

        dict = {piece.piece: piece.score for piece in proto.pieces[3:]}

        # Original monolingual vocab where `mask_token_id = len(vocab) - 1` 
        vocab = [
            (k, dict[k] if k in dict.keys() else 0.0) for k, v in self.original_tokenizer.fairseq_tokens_to_ids.items()
        ]

       # Extend the monolingual vocab with all remaining tokens from the pretrained XLM-R sentencepiece model.
        for piece in proto.pieces[3:]:
            if piece.piece not in self.original_tokenizer.fairseq_tokens_to_ids.keys():
                vocab += [(piece.piece, piece.score)]

        return vocab
```

